00:43:14 INFO   └─ [1;35muser answer:[0m [35mGood question. When categorizing attorneys by their visa focus, the classification should follow a priority order. An attorney who handles only one visa type should be classified as an "Exclusive Specialist" first. Then, if they don't meet that criterion, we check if their dominant visa type represents over 80% of their cases — if so, they're "Specialists." Only if neither of those conditions apply do we check if they work with 2-3 visa types to classify them as "Hybrid Practitioners." Everyone else falls into "Generalists." This cascading approach ensures there's no overlap — each attorney fits into exactly one category based on the first matching condition.[0m
