  raw: Which content groups, identified by their series identifiers, show good presence across different distribution setups? List those with sufficient coverage, including metrics that show how many distinct pieces of content belong to each group, how many different distribution tiers each group is available on, and add a column that shows the ratio of the number of distinct distribution tiers to the number of distinct content pieces for each franchise. Only include groups that have at least 3 distinct content pieces and are available on at least 3 distinct distribution tiers. Order the results by the number of distinct content pieces in descending order.

[Phase 1 SQL reference — use exact column names, thresholds, and formulas from this SQL where applicable]
SELECT c.series_id AS series_identifier,
       COUNT(DISTINCT c.content_key) AS distinct_content_pieces,
       COUNT(DISTINCT r.tiertype) AS distinct_distribution_tiers
FROM public.core AS c
JOIN public.show_rollups AS sr ON sr.srkeys = c.content_key
JOIN public.rollups AS r ON r.tierkey = sr.srlinks
GROUP BY c.series_id
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT c.content_key) >= 3
   AND COUNT(DISTINCT r.tiertype) >= 3
ORDER BY COUNT(DISTINCT c.content_key) DESC;
