  raw: Can you show how each access level (tier) contributes to the overall media collection? Please provide a structured output that includes each tier's ID number (`tierkey`), its name or type (`tiertype`), the total amount of media content it holds—measured by summing the video counts from all content available in that tier by aggregating the numeric `Videos_Total` values from `mediacounts->'content_volumes'`—their share of the entire catalog as a decimal ratio rounded to 4 decimal places (calculated as the tier's total videos divided by the total videos across all tiers), and additionally show how much HTML5-compatible content they contain and their HTML5 Depth Index. The output should rank the tiers from the highest to lowest total media content contribution.

[Phase 1 SQL reference — use exact column names, thresholds, and formulas from this SQL where applicable]
SELECT r.tierkey AS tier_id,
       r.tiertype AS tier_type,
       SUM(CASE WHEN ci.mediacounts->'content_volumes'->>'Videos_Total' ~ '^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$'
                THEN (ci.mediacounts->'content_volumes'->>'Videos_Total')::numeric ELSE 0 END) AS total_videos,
       ROUND(
         SUM(CASE WHEN ci.mediacounts->'content_volumes'->>'Videos_Total' ~ '^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$'
                  THEN (ci.mediacounts->'content_volumes'->>'Videos_Total')::numeric ELSE 0 END)
         / NULLIF(SUM(SUM(CASE WHEN ci.mediacounts->'content_volumes'->>'Videos_Total' ~ '^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$'
                  THEN (ci.mediacounts->'content_volumes'->>'Videos_Total')::numeric ELSE 0 END)) OVER (), 0),
       4) AS share_tier
FROM public.rollups AS r
JOIN public.show_rollups AS sr ON r.tierkey = sr.srlinks
JOIN public.content_info AS ci ON sr.srkeys = ci.content_key
GROUP BY r.tierkey, r.tiertype
ORDER BY total_videos DESC;

