A "Coordinated Influence Operation" in this context is defined by three key criteria that must all be met:

1. Cluster Size: The cluster must have more than 5 member accounts  
2. Coordination Score Threshold: The cluster's overall coordination score must exceed 0.8 (this comparison uses the cluster-level coordination score directly, not an aggregation of per-account coordination scores)  
3. Content Manipulation Rate: All member accounts in the cluster must demonstrate a Content Manipulation Score (CMS) above 0.7. The Content Manipulation Score (CMS) for each account is calculated as 0.4 times one minus the content uniqueness score (from the `content_quality` field within `content_metrics` in `content_activity` table), plus 0.3 times the media reuse ratio (from the `link_media` field within `content_metrics` in `content_activity` table), plus 0.3 times one minus the text uniqueness (the `TxtUniq` field in `interaction_metrics` table).

Only when all three conditions are satisfied simultaneously will the flag return "Yes". If any of these thresholds are not met, the result will be "No".

