07:05:18 INFO   └─ [1;35muser answer:[0m [35mThe "cumulative degradation percentage" in the electrical performance data represents the total percentage loss in panel efficiency that has accumulated over the entire operational lifetime of the plant since it went live. This is a cumulative metric that captures all degradation that has occurred up to the snapshot date.

To calculate the Annual Degradation Rate (ADR) for each plant, we need to annualize this cumulative degradation by dividing it by the number of years the plant has been operational. This gives us the average yearly degradation rate, which is distinct from the raw cumulative percentage. For example, a plant with 15% cumulative degradation over 5 years of operation would have an ADR of 3% per year.

This annualized rate is what we use in the financial impact calculation, as it allows us to project future revenue losses based on the expected degradation trajectory of each plant.[0m
